/target
egateway.conf
# ...and the log that appears beside it.  Running the binary from the repo
# root is an ordinary thing to do -- the live-gate runner points at
# `$REPO/transfer/CPM` -- and it left an untracked ethernetgateway.log every
# time.  The config was ignored and its log was not, which is the same file
# by a different name.
ethernetgateway.log
ethernetgateway.log.*
# The outbound SSH gateway's client key, generated on first use beside the
# config -- so running the binary from the repo root leaves one here, exactly
# as it leaves a config and a log.  Ignored above all because it is a PRIVATE
# key: untracked-but-not-ignored is how one gets committed by accident.  The
# web UI's public-key test renders the key-auth popup, which reaches
# `client_public_key_openssh` and generates it, so `cargo test` produces one too.
ethernet_gateway_ssh_key
# The SSH *server's* host key, by the same argument.
ethernet_ssh_host_key
*.swp
*.swo
*~
